Repair only the supplied scientific or grammatical issues. Return {sections:[{id:number,patches:[{before:string,after:string,issueIndex:number}],reason:string}]}. Include each supplied section exactly once. Use exact unique substrings in its candidate. At most 3 non-overlapping patches per section; their combined BEFORE text must cover at most 35% of that section. issueIndex refers to that section's issues. Keep wording elsewhere unchanged. Restore the original meaning, uncertainty and proposal status. No extra style pass. If bounded repairs cannot solve the issues, return patches:[] and explain.
INPUT DATA:
{"sections": [{"id": 5, "heading": "Limitations and Conclusion", "original": "An abstention rule may make the limits of the evidence clearer while leaving a less complete map. A local inventory may also contain outdated boundaries. The proposed experiment will therefore not estimate annual retreat rates or establish that any particular glacier is shrinking [S2]. Its contribution would be a more explicit account of what the available images can support.", "candidate": "An abstention rule may make the limits of the evidence clearer, but it will leave a less complete map. A local inventory might contain outdated boundaries, as no field measurements have been collected for this proposal [S1]. The proposed experiment will not estimate annual retreat rates or establish that any particular glacier is shrinking [S2]. Instead, its contribution will be a more explicit account of what the available images can support.", "issues": [{"originalQuote": "An abstention rule may make the limits of the evidence clearer while leaving a less complete map.", "revisedQuote": "An abstention rule may make the limits of the evidence clearer, but it will leave a less complete map.", "problem": "Changes a possible tradeoff into a definite prediction that the map will be less complete."}, {"originalQuote": "A local inventory may also contain outdated boundaries.", "revisedQuote": "A local inventory might contain outdated boundaries, as no field measurements have been collected for this proposal [S1].", "problem": "Adds an unsupported causal connection: the absence of field measurements for this proposal does not explain whether the inventory boundaries are outdated."}, {"originalQuote": "Its contribution would be a more explicit account of what the available images can support.", "revisedQuote": "Instead, its contribution will be a more explicit account of what the available images can support.", "problem": "Replaces a conditional proposed contribution with a definite outcome, weakening the original uncertainty."}]}], "sources": [{"id": "S1", "title": "Controlled source packet: domain and evidence brief", "excerpt": "The proposed glacier study uses optical imagery from two summer visits. Cloud-covered pixels are unavailable observations, not ice-free terrain. A local inventory supplies glacier outlines but does not establish recent retreat. No field measurements have been collected for this proposal.", "content_kind": "author_constructed_evaluation_fixture"}, {"id": "S2", "title": "Controlled source packet: experimental design brief", "excerpt": "A boundary model will receive the same image pairs in both conditions. The comparison is between mandatory classification and an abstention rule for cloud-covered pixels. The evaluation set will contain 24 image pairs. The study will not estimate annual retreat rates.", "content_kind": "author_constructed_evaluation_fixture"}]}
